1
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,280
So I'm turning up high and
happens with myự ramen.

2
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:08,660
I'm slipping away from the moment.

3
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:13,360
No problem drawing around the world.

4
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:17,480
I'm burning very selesophantan!

5
00:01:18,740 --> 00:01:24,260
Until step, I'm turning in my face.

6
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,240
Oh

7
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:56,170
Gear?

8
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:58,006
Your techniques have changed?

9
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:00,457
Are you supposed to be a steam engine?

10
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:02,540
You certainly are full of hot air.

11
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:05,200
You're starting to test my patience.

12
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:13,760
The truth is, I'm glad I
met you guys when I did.

13
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:17,180
Come, come!

14
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:22,940
What, are you stopping to aim?

15
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:25,695
That only gives me more time to dodge.

16
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:27,610
Fine.

17
00:02:27,693 --> 00:02:31,500
Let's see how good your aim is,
then. Shake! Shake, crystal!

18
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:44,950
Rifle!

19
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:54,117
Huh?

20
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:56,300
I can't see him at all!

21
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:04,960
It's fair!

22
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:08,380
Missile!

23
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:19,940
Impossible!

24
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:26,820
No, it has to be.

25
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,817
The truth is...

26
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:31,420
I'm glad I met you guys when I did.

27
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:33,544
He's using the shave technique.

28
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:38,400
Only CP9 should know the six powers,
but he's clearly mastered it.

29
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,120
Air door!

30
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:45,590
Huh?

31
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:47,900
He disappeared.

32
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,340
This is unheard of.

33
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:53,337
A pirate commanding one of our techniques?

34
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:55,320
This is a sick joke.

35
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,140
Don't tell me he was
capable of this all along.

36
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:03,620
No, it doesn't matter.

37
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:07,280
No one can match the speed
of a true six powers master.

38
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:09,220
I won't lose to him!

39
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:14,197
If I turn his body parts
into doors like before,

40
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:16,660
that should stop him dead in his tracks.

41
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:20,100
After that, all I have
to do is finish him off.

42
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:32,237
When we fought before, and it
looked like you were disappearing?

43
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:36,320
You were really just moving your
feet ten or twenty times a second!

44
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:38,577
I got the hang of it too.

45
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:42,484
But I never would have figured
something like that out on my own.

46
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:48,017
I can take it!

47
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:50,080
I'll use my strongest defense.

48
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:12,017
You sure are tough! Aren't you?

49
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:18,897
All right, then I was gonna save
it, but I have an even better trick.

50
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:20,120
Don't blink.

51
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:25,500
I call this...

52
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:38,700
Man, I'm beat.

53
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:41,860
Guess my body can't keep this up for long.

54
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:47,140
Well, I don't care
about my body right now.

55
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,780
I need to move ahead.

56
00:05:57,920 --> 00:05:58,750
Damn it!

57
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,155
What's going on here?

58
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:02,160
Quick, fire the cannons, man!

59
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:03,840
Before they step on us!

60
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:06,480
Yeah, nice try!

61
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:09,197
Put those pea shooters
on enough to stop me!

62
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:13,927
You can ride or you can fight, little
bit, but we're coming through either way!

63
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:18,177
I see it, and I still can't believe it.

64
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:22,557
I don't know what you said to those guys,
but it must have been something else.

65
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:24,640
We warriors understand each other.

66
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:26,967
The time has come, brothers.

67
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:29,712
The courthouse is looming on the horizon.

68
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:30,770
Onward!

69
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:33,760
What are you doing?

70
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:35,980
Hurry up and go inside already.

71
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:38,577
The pirates are in the
courthouse, aren't they?

72
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:39,490
Yeah,

73
00:06:39,573 --> 00:06:42,677
but the problem is there's a big frog at
the door and he's not letting anyone in.

74
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:43,590
A frog?

75
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:47,797
Keep hiding, Yokozuna.

76
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:49,120
Go get him an edge!

77
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:52,446
We can't stop until the
drawbridge comes down!

78
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:56,397
If those guys break our line in the
fence, thousands of them can pour in here!

79
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:57,310
Get out!

80
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:04,958
Only one of us needs to get through!

81
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:09,591
Even if everyone else falls, as long
as someone pulls that lever, we've won!

82
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:21,020
You okay, sis?

83
00:07:21,780 --> 00:07:23,080
Don't worry about me.

84
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:25,457
All that matters is bringing
down that bridge and

85
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:28,017
making sure the Straw Hats
get to the Tower of Law.

86
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:28,930
Hold it!

87
00:07:29,013 --> 00:07:30,077
You're not going anywhere!

88
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,520
Oh, yeah? Try it! Stop it!

89
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:39,742
What are those pirates plotting?

90
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:42,497
Why is it so important
for them to go upstairs?

91
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:43,410
Huh?

92
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:47,397
You won't get an answer out of me!

93
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:48,980
We'll see about that,

94
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:53,022
but I tell you one thing you're
gonna pay if you hurt our big bro!

95
00:07:55,660 --> 00:07:56,540
After them!

96
00:07:56,860 --> 00:07:58,560
Bring those pirates down!

97
00:07:58,940 --> 00:08:03,822
How many of these stupid guards are we
gonna have to beat before they catch a hint?

98
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:06,160
There they are! Attack!

99
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:13,125
Hey, if you have to throw them,
at least don't throw them at me!

100
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,417
Would you guys shut up?

101
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:21,971
I'm trying to think here.

102
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:24,394
Must have taken a wrong turn somewhere.

103
00:08:33,420 --> 00:08:37,217
You want us to take Franky and Nico
Robin to the Gates of Justice now?

104
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:38,540
Yes! Do it! Quickly!

105
00:08:38,980 --> 00:08:40,577
But we're way ahead of schedule.

106
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:42,397
The escort ship isn't even ready yet.

107
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,380
I don't care.

108
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:46,357
We can just wait for it on
the other side of the gates.

109
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:50,237
If we get rid of those two, the pirates
won't have a reason to fight anymore.

110
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:52,337
There's no point in risking
another battle with those

111
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:55,457
monsters when we have the
power to end this right now.

112
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:59,620
And while you're at it, gather
all the members of CP9, too. Sir!

113
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:09,944
Now, it seems as if your one-way trip to
hell will be departing ahead of schedule.

114
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:14,321
Then we'll have all the time in
the world to deal with your friends

115
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:21,737
Those pirates sure know how to
bring the party, don't they?

116
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:25,417
I don't know if they have common
sense, but they sure as heck have guts.

117
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,437
Just you wait and watch, Chimney!

118
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:28,460
In the end,

119
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:32,557
whether they live or die, that straw
hat boy and all of his little friends?

120
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:35,117
Are going to shake things
up the whole world over!

121
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:38,997
In hundreds of years, nobody's
pulled a stunt like this one.

122
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:41,040
Mark my words,

123
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:42,891
when this battle is over,

124
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:47,980
every man, woman and child is gonna
know the name of Straw Hat Luffy!

125
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,110
Robin!

126
00:10:00,620 --> 00:10:02,160
Yeah, you made it!

127
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:05,270
Luffy...

128
00:10:05,353 --> 00:10:07,340
I'm here to save you!

129
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,518
Chief Spandam, sir!

130
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,357
There's a man in a straw
hat standing on the

131
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:16,017
courthouse rooftop who's
shouting things at Nico Robin.

132
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:19,737
I wasn't able to confirm his identity
up close, but I assume it must be Luffy.

133
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:20,702
On the rooftop?

134
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:24,277
How could that happen when I saw
Pluno up there just a second ago?

135
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:26,340
I thought he was keeping watch.

136
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,400
That idiot.

137
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:29,169
What the hell is he doing?

138
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:37,591
Guess I've been running around a lot, huh?

139
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:40,360
And time for a snack.

140
00:10:40,860 --> 00:10:42,740
Good thing I came prepared.

141
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,380
Me time!

142
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:53,700
I knew putting these in my
pockets was a good idea.

143
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:56,800
I just wish I had more pockets.

144
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:05,320
So that's him, Haas, Straw Hat Luffy.

145
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:08,060
But what the hell is going on here?

146
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:10,800
If Bluno was up there, he should've...

147
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:15,040
It can't be.

148
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:16,840
No, he couldn't have.

149
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:23,580
Bluno's a member of CP9, a six powers
master with Devil Fruit powers, no less.

150
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:25,820
His power level is superhuman.

151
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:30,100
All right, ready for round two.

152
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:33,740
How could that scrawny
brat ever defeat him?

153
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:42,100
Chase Fondam, sir, how should we proceed?

154
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:44,660
Lucci, where is he?

155
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:49,400
Somebody call him now,
and the rest of CB9, too.

156
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:50,819
I've heard enough.

157
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,777
I won't be satisfied until they wipe out

158
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:54,977
Straw Hat and everyone
in his wretched crew.

159
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:55,890
No!

160
00:11:55,973 --> 00:11:56,803
While you're at it,

161
00:11:56,886 --> 00:11:59,857
tell Baskerville that if he lets
the Straw Hats lower that bridge,

162
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:02,417
I'm going to send all
three of his heads rolling!

163
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,330
Yes, sir!

164
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:09,940
Hey, get that chin up, Nico Robin.

165
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:15,046
You know, most people wouldn't
come here to save their friends.

166
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:18,699
Hell, most people couldn't
even make it here at all.

167
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:20,157
Don't get me wrong.

168
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:22,437
I know the only reason you agreed to the

169
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:24,977
government's terms was so
you could protect them.

170
00:12:25,060 --> 00:12:26,197
But you saw what happened.

171
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:30,398
They don't give a damn about keeping
their word to you or anyone else.

172
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:31,940
The deal is shot.

173
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:35,757
Even if you keep your end of the
bargain, it's not going to help anyone.

174
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:39,617
Only thing left is to wait for your
crew to break you out of this dump.

175
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:41,300
Doesn't sound so bad to me.

176
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:45,900
And yet, here you are,
looking as miserable as ever.

177
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:51,282
I get the feeling you're running from
something even your friends don't know about.

178
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:55,632
I Wouldn't worry about the
Straw Hats dying in this place.

179
00:12:55,800 --> 00:13:00,506
But if you can't look him in the eye in
the end, they won't be able to save you.

180
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:11,420
Well, whether you like it or
not I'm gonna make you face.

181
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:19,117
Listen up all of you we're putting Nico
Robin out of Straw Hats reach immediately.

182
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,376
Come with me to the Gates of Justice.

183
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:22,676
Bring the prisoners.

184
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:23,780
But, but chief.

185
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:26,640
No buts, just do it.

186
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:31,376
Well, uh, there's one giant
butt that's a big problem.

187
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:33,760
What the hell is that?

188
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:36,700
Oh, hey, Spanda.

189
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,877
Like you said, I'm pretty much screwed.

190
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:41,657
So I figured I might as well
blow myself up, you know?

191
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:42,570
What?

192
00:13:42,653 --> 00:13:46,177
That way at least I get to take
your sorry ass with me when I go.

193
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:47,090
You fool.

194
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:48,797
Wait a minute, will you?

195
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:52,777
If my butt goes off, the explosion's
going to be at least a mile wide.

196
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:55,978
Not much point in running,
but you might as well try.

197
00:13:56,180 --> 00:14:00,180
I don't know what's going on in
your pants, but please make it stop!

198
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,237
Three, two...

199
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,732
Damn it, I can't die in a time like this!

200
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:07,810
One...

201
00:14:07,893 --> 00:14:08,723
Stop it!

202
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:13,020
Time to go, Robin.

203
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:17,480
Coo-dip!

204
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:24,730
Good.

205
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:26,608
The chains are broken, too.

206
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:28,980
We're following!

207
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:32,400
You burn!

208
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:46,640
That was a close one.

209
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:50,242
Good thing that fence was
there to catch us, huh?

210
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:53,301
Hey, you didn't get hurt, did ya?

211
00:14:57,980 --> 00:14:59,617
If I had another bottle of cola,

212
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:02,759
I could get us to the other
side with a coup de vin.

213
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:05,180
Hey, check it out.

214
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:06,693
Straw Hat's over there.

215
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:08,279
Now's your chance.

216
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:10,037
Better give him your answer.

217
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,840
He tricked us! Chief!

218
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:15,777
Franky and Nico Robin broke the
chains and went out on the balcony!

219
00:15:15,860 --> 00:15:18,040
Then what are you waiting for stupid?

220
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:19,497
Capture them already.

221
00:15:19,580 --> 00:15:23,051
If you let them get away, I'll
send you all to the gallows!

222
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:24,470
What?!

223
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:33,750
Hey! Robin!

224
00:15:33,833 --> 00:15:35,040
You're still there!

225
00:15:35,340 --> 00:15:36,928
Didn't you hear me yelling?

226
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:39,730
Reef...

227
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:40,643
Don't let them get away!

228
00:15:40,726 --> 00:15:41,997
Grab them before they run!

229
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:44,377
I don't have time for you thugs right now!

230
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:45,360
Weapons left!

231
00:15:49,060 --> 00:15:51,413
I guess that means Frankie's there, too.

232
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:53,220
Okay, I'll be right over.

233
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:57,120
It's a little far, but I can make it.

234
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:04,660
Come, come!

235
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:06,500
Stop it!

236
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:15,720
How many times do I have to tell you?

237
00:16:15,860 --> 00:16:17,120
I'm not coming back.

238
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:19,340
I'm not part of your crew anymore.

239
00:16:19,540 --> 00:16:20,700
Just go away.

240
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:22,857
I don't want to see your face ever again.

241
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:23,937
Don't you understand?

242
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:26,297
Why did you come to save
me in the first place?

243
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:28,086
Why can't you just let me go?

244
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:31,040
You never asked for this.

245
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:33,360
You've gone too far.

246
00:16:33,780 --> 00:16:35,200
For the last time.

247
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:37,280
I don't want you here.

248
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:49,000
Do you hear me I just want to die.

249
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:57,040
Now this is entertainment what a twist!

250
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:00,857
What the hell are you trying to pull your

251
00:17:00,940 --> 00:17:02,997
friends put their lives
on the line to come here?

252
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:03,910
And you...

253
00:17:03,993 --> 00:17:05,697
They decided to do that on their own.

254
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:06,717
Are you kidding me?

255
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:07,630
Who cares?

256
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:13,060
You're in the way.

257
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:17,160
What's wrong, Kaku?

258
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:18,760
Fitting your anger?

